    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green with the only concrete test class (`AcceptanceTest`) passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived, read-only `telephoneDisplay` field to the owner response: the stored E.164 `telephone` formatted for humans, while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\nFollowing the existing pattern for derived owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `locality`, etc.), I made three changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a standalone helper (kept off the mapper interface so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit `String\u2192String` mapping method, matching the `Locality`/`AgeBand` convention) that formats E.164 into `country code + space + national digits grouped in threes`. It splits the country code using the same known-country table as the E.164 normaliser (`+61`\u21929 national digits, `+1`\u219210, longest-prefix first), with a two-digit fallback for unrecognised codes, then groups national digits in threes. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression wiring `telephoneDisplay` to `TelephoneDisplay.of(owner.getTelephone())`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` passes: input `0412 345 678` stores `telephone` as `+61412345678` and returns `telephoneDisplay` as `+61 412 345 678`.",
